# Narrow diagnostic and deterministic schedule candidate

ADR.md was written before the fixture. There is no production startup/admission fix.

Only the Host safe opt-in diagnostic block changes in production source. It calls the existing engine-only inspectDrain to observe real pre-close OLE registration, counters and status. vendorFailed is true only for a valid FAILED status, false only for a valid OK status, otherwise null. All original readiness, ACK, native-entry, geometry, queue, return and cleanup behavior remains unchanged. Token/HWND/thread/content are not exposed; nonAtomic=true remains explicit.

w2-main.cpp is a private fresh-copy delta from sealed W2d8 main. Successful completion now collects the same bounded diagnostic only when startup opt-in is enabled; the original failure branch and all browser/native/permission assertions remain exact. It does not change historical packets or outputs.

The actual DLL/SDK fixture has three real ordered schedules, one EXE and three TIMEOUT20 serial CTests. A mutex test command lane holds the real engine between commands; the original SetTimer-produced UI callback runs unchanged. The actual SDK hooks decide admission. The ACK's real DragHandle identity cancellation continuation is retained, so registration-specific and total completion counts are distinct.

Default runs require real registration. Current B/C observations produce a complete report and natural return2 after actual safe teardown; explicit --characterize is an observation contract only. Every record still marks startup/full qualification false. Any unresolved owner or timeout calls ExitProcess91 rather than unsafe unwind. Root owns actual execution and Owned closure.

The input ledger binds 24 current normal SDK CPP, 15 private headers, 32 public headers and the supporting ABI/vendor sources. It contains hashes, not copied production algorithms. No compiler/native/Node/CMake or author loader evaluation occurred. No live/index/branch/other candidate write occurred.

copy-plan.json binds eight small payloads, two exact source inputs, and the two disjoint diagnostic byte intervals. Outside bytes and original encodings replay exactly. A current Host source pin deliberately does not accept the candidate Host implicitly: Root must derive a fresh actual input pin if adopting that observation before compiling the fixture.

Same-size WM_SIZE filtering is insufficient because genuine geometry and main-document epoch transitions can also cancel registration. The conditional registration-fence design remains in ADR.md pending actual schedule/first-rejection evidence; it is not implemented here.
